                        "entry_id": "7f19e1fa-4fa8-3927-8f82-08a27b5570de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large lake trout, Salvelinus namaycush, found mainly in Canada and northern areas of the US."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "73a2de67-f145-44e4-a78c-8a6804d233b4",
                                "sense_id": "e801809b-f65b-3177-936d-4f56a9c062d2",
                                "text": "In Long Lake there are plenty of tuladi (salmon trout) and trout. […] I have caught tuladi running as high as sixteen pounds in the Fish River Lakes. The tuladi in Long Lake are the best, always fat. There are two kinds of tuladi; the one with the white belly is poorer than that which has spots on its belly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07eb0be0-bc3a-4202-b1eb-88b63c5b51ef",
                                "sense_id": "e801809b-f65b-3177-936d-4f56a9c062d2",
                                "text": "[…] a narrow sheet of water, about 22 M. long, abounding in large-sized trout and 'tuladi', a heavy fish of the salmon family."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
